From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:48:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop2: Set up the overlay from a list of windows

The overlay setup of a video port takes its windows and their plane
states from the planes of its CRTC, and the layers of each video port
from the layers distributed to it at bind time. To blend the windows of
one CRTC in two video ports, the overlay setup needs to take windows
that aren't the windows of the planes, and the layer split between the
video ports needs to change at runtime.

Pass the windows to blend and the plane states they show to the layer
mixer and alpha setup, and keep the layers each video port currently
has in OVL_PORT_SEL in ovl_layers, protected by ovl_lock. No functional
change.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
